# Official ruling: Elusive Otter's power is compared to a blocker's only as blockers are declared (CR 509.1b); once it has
# been legally blocked, changing power does not undo the block. Llanowar Elves (power 1) legally blocks the 1/1 Otter; Bot1
# then casts Lightning Bolt at Bot2, a noncreature spell, and prowess makes the Otter 2/2 (CR 702.108a). The Elves still block it:
# the Otter kills them and survives with 1 damage, and Bot2 takes only the Bolt's 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Elusive Otter
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Elusive Otter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Elusive Otter > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves > Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter.Power = 2

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Elusive Otter.Damage = 1
